<title>SWEDEN: Swedish PM says to boost jobs in spring budget.</title>
<headline>Swedish PM says to boost jobs in spring budget.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Prime Minister Goran Persson said on Wednesday that the government would present a package of subsidised jobs in the spring budget in a bid to lower unemployment.</p>
<p>Sweden's unemployment rate is running near 8.7 percent, or about 12-13 percent including people on government work schemes.</p>
<p>Persson told reporters after a political parties' leaders debate in parliament that this would be the next government move to address unemployment.</p>
<p>&quot;There really will be no opportunity for that before the spring budget,&quot; Persson said.</p>
<p>Persson last year pledged to halve unemployment by the next general election in 1998.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
